{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-57622","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67179","text":"Runefort Protocol — v0.1"}]},{"id":"blk-57623","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67180","marks":["bold"],"text":"A layout protocol for living, file-backed, tile-grid web apps."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57625","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67181","marks":["bold"],"text":"Part of the [&] Protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-67182","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-67183","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-67184","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-67185","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/THREE_PROTOCOL_STACK.md"}],"text":"Three-protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-67186","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-67187","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"}]}],"id":"blk-57624","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-57626","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67188","text":"Status: draft v0.1 Owner: runefort.com Date: 2026-04-25 Position: protocol-level. Independent of [&], PULSE, PRISM. May be used by them; does not require them."}]},{"id":"blk-57627","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67189","marks":["bold"],"text":"Related documents:"}]},{"id":"blk-57628","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57630","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67190","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.core.md"}],"text":"@runefort/core — Reference Web Component Framework v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-57629","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57632","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67191","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.dsl.md"}],"text":".rune DSL — v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-57631","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57634","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67192","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-BUILD-ORDER.md"}],"text":"Interactive Layer — Build Order"}]}],"id":"blk-57633","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57636","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67193","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-1_BYOK.md"}],"text":"RFort-1 — BYOK Modal + OpenRouter Key Storage"}]}],"id":"blk-57635","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57638","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67194","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-2_MCP.md"}],"text":"RFort-2 — MCP Proxy + Client + Connection Panel"}]}],"id":"blk-57637","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57640","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67195","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-3_CHAT.md"}],"text":"RFort-3 — Chat Panel with Fort-Aware Navigation"}]}],"id":"blk-57639","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57642","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67196","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-4_TOKENFLOWS.md"}],"text":"RFort-4 — Token Flow Animations on Edges"}]}],"id":"blk-57641","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57644","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67197","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-5_REPO_IMPORT.md"}],"text":"RFort-5 — Repo Import → Fort Generator"}]}],"id":"blk-57643","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57646","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67198","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-6_WORKSPACES.md"}],"text":"RFort-6 — Workspace Switcher + Supabase Persistence"}]}],"id":"blk-57645","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57647","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67199","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57648","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67200","text":"0. What this is, in one paragraph"}]},{"id":"blk-57649","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67201","text":"Runefort is a small declarative protocol for describing a "},{"id":"spn-67202","marks":["bold"],"text":"tiled, file-backed UI layout"},{"id":"spn-67203","text":". You declare *rooms* (tiles), *claims* (file-system regions each room owns), *neighbors* (adjacency for navigation), and *state bindings* (how live state colors a tile). A conformant renderer compiles the declaration to a CSS grid, surfaces each claim's content for inline viewing or editing, and overlays live state. The protocol is the contract between the declaration and the renderer. Nothing more."}]},{"id":"blk-57650","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67204","text":"It is not a workforce platform. It is not a supervisor framework. It is not a graph visualization library. It is the "},{"id":"spn-67205","marks":["bold"],"text":"layout language"},{"id":"spn-67206","text":" that those things can be built with."}]},{"id":"blk-57651","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67207","text":"1. Why a protocol (not a library)"}]},{"id":"blk-57652","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57654","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67208","marks":["bold"],"text":"Renderer-portable."},{"id":"spn-67209","text":" The same "},{"id":"spn-67210","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-67211","text":" should render in Elixir/Phoenix, TypeScript/React, or static HTML. The protocol is the only thing they share."}]}],"id":"blk-57653","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57656","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67212","marks":["bold"],"text":"Diffable."},{"id":"spn-67213","text":" Layouts live in version control as text. Reviews become readable. SVG graph layouts cannot do this."}]}],"id":"blk-57655","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57658","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67214","marks":["bold"],"text":"Extensible by composition."},{"id":"spn-67215","text":" Apps add *vocabularies* (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-67216","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor"},{"id":"spn-67217","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67218","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard"},{"id":"spn-67219","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67220","marks":["code"],"text":"wiki-page"},{"id":"spn-67221","text":") on top of the core primitives. The protocol does not know about supervisors."}]}],"id":"blk-57657","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57660","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67222","marks":["bold"],"text":"No runtime layout engine required."},{"id":"spn-67223","text":" All layout is compile-time deterministic. No d3, no dagre, no jitter."}]}],"id":"blk-57659","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57661","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67224","text":"2. Core primitives"}]},{"id":"blk-57662","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67225","text":"Four primitives. That is the entire vocabulary."}]},{"id":"blk-57663","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67226","text":"2.1 Room"}]},{"id":"blk-57664","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67227","text":"A room is a tile in the grid. It has an id, a position, a size, and arbitrary metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-57665","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"id\": \"memory\",\n  \"position\": [0, 0],\n  \"size\": [3, 2],\n  \"label\": \"memory.ex\",\n  \"meta\": {}\n}"},{"id":"blk-57666","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67228","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-67229","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-67230","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-67231","text":" are integer cell coordinates in a CSS grid. "},{"id":"spn-67232","marks":["code"],"text":"[0,0]"},{"id":"spn-67233","text":" is top-left. "},{"id":"spn-67234","marks":["code"],"text":"size: [3,2]"},{"id":"spn-67235","text":" means 3 columns wide, 2 rows tall. The renderer is free to choose the cell pixel size; the protocol only specifies cell counts."}]},{"id":"blk-57667","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67236","text":"2.2 Claim"}]},{"id":"blk-57668","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67237","text":"A claim is a file-system region a room \"owns.\" A renderer uses claims to (a) list which files belong to a room and (b) surface those files inline — either as a viewer or an editor — when the user activates the room. Optional behaviors include generating external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-67238","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-67239","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67240","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-67241","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67242","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-67243","text":") for users who prefer their own tools."}]},{"id":"blk-57669","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"pattern\": \"lib/my_app/memory/**/*.ex\",\n  \"anchor\": \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex#L24\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-57670","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67244","marks":["code"],"text":"pattern"},{"id":"spn-67245","text":" is a glob. "},{"id":"spn-67246","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-67247","text":" is the canonical file the room represents (the one a click on the tile opens)."}]},{"id":"blk-57671","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67248","text":"2.3 Neighbor"}]},{"id":"blk-57672","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67249","text":"A neighbor declares an adjacency between two rooms. Neighbors drive keyboard navigation ("},{"id":"spn-67250","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-67251","text":"), focus order, and may be rendered as connecting lines."}]},{"id":"blk-57673","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"from\": \"memory\", \"to\": \"deploy\", \"kind\": \"adjacent\" }"},{"id":"blk-57674","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67252","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-67253","text":" is one of: "},{"id":"spn-67254","marks":["code"],"text":"adjacent"},{"id":"spn-67255","text":" (touching), "},{"id":"spn-67256","marks":["code"],"text":"linked"},{"id":"spn-67257","text":" (logical link, may not be touching), "},{"id":"spn-67258","marks":["code"],"text":"nested"},{"id":"spn-67259","text":" (one contains the other)."}]},{"id":"blk-57675","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67260","text":"2.4 State binding"}]},{"id":"blk-57676","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67261","text":"A state binding tells the renderer how to color a room based on a runtime signal. The protocol defines the *binding*, not the signal source — signals are pushed to the renderer over whatever transport the host app provides (WebSocket, SSE, polling, static)."}]},{"id":"blk-57677","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"signal\": \"kappa\",\n  \"thresholds\": [\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.3\", \"class\": \"cold\" },\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.6\", \"class\": \"warm\" },\n    { \"if\": \">= 0.6\", \"class\": \"hot\" }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-57678","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67262","marks":["code"],"text":"class"},{"id":"spn-67263","text":" is a token the renderer maps to CSS. The protocol reserves five canonical classes: "},{"id":"spn-67264","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-67265","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67266","marks":["code"],"text":"warm"},{"id":"spn-67267","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67268","marks":["code"],"text":"hot"},{"id":"spn-67269","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67270","marks":["code"],"text":"fault"},{"id":"spn-67271","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67272","marks":["code"],"text":"idle"},{"id":"spn-67273","text":". Apps may add custom classes — renderers should ignore unknown classes gracefully (treat as "},{"id":"spn-67274","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-67275","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-57679","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67276","text":"3. Document shape"}]},{"id":"blk-57680","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67277","text":"A complete "},{"id":"spn-67278","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-67279","text":" is just an object containing arrays of the four primitives, plus header metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-57681","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"title\": \"my_app forge floor\",\n  \"grid\": { \"columns\": 6, \"rows\": 4 },\n  \"rooms\": [ ... ],\n  \"claims\": [ ... ],\n  \"neighbors\": [ ... ],\n  \"state_bindings\": [ ... ],\n  \"vocabulary\": \"core\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-57682","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67280","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.columns"},{"id":"spn-67281","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-67282","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.rows"},{"id":"spn-67283","text":" are the total grid dimensions. "},{"id":"spn-67284","marks":["code"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-67285","text":" is the name of the extension vocabulary in use; "},{"id":"spn-67286","marks":["code"],"text":"\"core\""},{"id":"spn-67287","text":" means no extensions."}]},{"id":"blk-57683","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67288","text":"4. The DSL surface (host-language sugar)"}]},{"id":"blk-57684","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67289","text":"Hosts may expose a DSL that compiles to the JSON above. The DSL is "},{"id":"spn-67290","marks":["bold"],"text":"not normative"},{"id":"spn-67291","text":" — only the JSON is. A reference Elixir DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-57685","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"defmodule MyApp.Floor do\n  use Runefort.Layout, columns: 6, rows: 4\n\n  room :memory,\n    at: {0, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/memory/},\n    anchor: \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex:24\"\n\n  room :deploy,\n    at: {3, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/deploy/}\n\n  neighbors :memory => :deploy\n\n  bind :memory, signal: :kappa,\n    cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\"\nend"},{"id":"blk-57686","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67292","text":"A reference TypeScript DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-57687","kind":"code","language":"ts","text":"const floor = layout({ columns: 6, rows: 4 }, [\n  room(\"memory\", { at: [0,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/memory/**\" }),\n  room(\"deploy\", { at: [3,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/deploy/**\" }),\n  neighbor(\"memory\", \"deploy\"),\n  bind(\"memory\", \"kappa\", { cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\" }),\n]);"},{"id":"blk-57688","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67293","text":"Both compile to the same JSON. Either is conformant. Neither is privileged."}]},{"id":"blk-57689","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67294","text":"5. Renderer contract"}]},{"id":"blk-57690","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67295","text":"A conformant renderer MUST:"}]},{"id":"blk-57691","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67296","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-67297","marks":["bold"],"text":"Layout."},{"id":"spn-67298","text":" Render rooms in a CSS grid (or visually equivalent) using each room's "},{"id":"spn-67299","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-67300","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-67301","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-67302","text":". The grid MUST be deterministic — given the same JSON, the rendered DOM order MUST be stable. 2. "},{"id":"spn-67303","marks":["bold"],"text":"Anchors."},{"id":"spn-67304","text":" Resolve each room's "},{"id":"spn-67305","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-67306","text":" to its content (the file or content region the room represents). Activating a tile MUST surface that content — by default, inline within the host page (viewer or editor). Renderers MAY additionally offer an external-editor handoff URL as a secondary action, but inline surfacing is the canonical behavior. 3. "},{"id":"spn-67307","marks":["bold"],"text":"State classes."},{"id":"spn-67308","text":" Apply CSS classes from "},{"id":"spn-67309","marks":["code"],"text":"state_bindings"},{"id":"spn-67310","text":" to each room's root element. Class names MUST be predictable: "},{"id":"spn-67311","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-cold"},{"id":"spn-67312","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67313","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-hot"},{"id":"spn-67314","text":", etc. 4. "},{"id":"spn-67315","marks":["bold"],"text":"Accessibility."},{"id":"spn-67316","text":" Each room MUST be focusable (keyboard) and have a stable accessible name (the room's "},{"id":"spn-67317","marks":["code"],"text":"label"},{"id":"spn-67318","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-67319","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-67320","text":"). 5. "},{"id":"spn-67321","marks":["bold"],"text":"Neighbor navigation."},{"id":"spn-67322","text":" Arrow keys (or "},{"id":"spn-67323","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-67324","text":") MUST move focus along "},{"id":"spn-67325","marks":["code"],"text":"neighbor"},{"id":"spn-67326","text":" edges. Renderers MAY also expose mouse navigation; keyboard support is required."}]},{"id":"blk-57692","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67327","text":"A conformant renderer SHOULD:"}]},{"id":"blk-57693","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57695","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67328","text":"Provide an inline editor (not just a read-only viewer) for the focused room's "},{"id":"spn-67329","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-67330","text":" when the host environment supports text editing."}]}],"id":"blk-57694","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57697","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67331","text":"Highlight neighbor adjacencies on hover/focus."}]}],"id":"blk-57696","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57699","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67332","text":"Re-render on signal change without full reload."}]}],"id":"blk-57698","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57700","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67333","text":"A conformant renderer MAY:"}]},{"id":"blk-57701","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57703","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67334","text":"Add domain-specific vocabularies (see §6)."}]}],"id":"blk-57702","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57705","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67335","text":"Display additional metadata from "},{"id":"spn-67336","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-67337","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-57704","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57707","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67338","text":"Animate state class transitions."}]}],"id":"blk-57706","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57709","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67339","text":"Offer external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-67340","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-67341","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67342","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-67343","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67344","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-67345","text":") as a secondary action for users who prefer their own tools. Renderers that run outside the browser (e.g. static-site generators, server-rendered HTML with no JS) MAY treat handoff as their primary surfacing strategy and still claim conformance."}]}],"id":"blk-57708","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57710","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67346","text":"6. Vocabularies (extension points)"}]},{"id":"blk-57711","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67347","text":"The protocol's core knows nothing about supervisors, dashboards, or wikis. Apps declare a *vocabulary* — a named bundle of extra fields on "},{"id":"spn-67348","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-67349","text":", extra signals, and extra state classes."}]},{"id":"blk-57712","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"vocabulary\": \"supervisor-floor.v1\",\n  \"rooms\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"memory\",\n      \"position\": [0,0], \"size\": [3,2],\n      \"meta\": {\n        \"supervisor\": {\n          \"autonomy\": \"advise\",\n          \"uptime_seconds\": 957840,\n          \"last_action\": \"consolidated 47 nodes\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-57713","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67350","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-67351","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-67352","text":" vocabulary defines what "},{"id":"spn-67353","marks":["code"],"text":"meta.supervisor"},{"id":"spn-67354","text":" contains. A renderer that doesn't know "},{"id":"spn-67355","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-67356","text":" MUST still render the layout correctly — it just won't display the supervisor-specific overlay. "},{"id":"spn-67357","marks":["bold"],"text":"Vocabulary unknown = degrade, don't fail."}]},{"id":"blk-57714","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67358","text":"Reserved vocabularies (managed by the protocol authors):"}]},{"id":"blk-57715","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57717","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67359","marks":["code"],"text":"core"},{"id":"spn-67360","text":" — the four primitives, no extensions."}]}],"id":"blk-57716","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57719","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67361","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-67362","text":" — for [&]/Runefort supervisor workforce apps."}]}],"id":"blk-57718","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57721","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67363","marks":["code"],"text":"codebase-atlas.v1"},{"id":"spn-67364","text":" — for repository visualization apps."}]}],"id":"blk-57720","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57723","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67365","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard-grid.v1"},{"id":"spn-67366","text":" — for metric/observability tile dashboards."}]}],"id":"blk-57722","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57724","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67367","text":"Custom vocabularies are namespaced freely ("},{"id":"spn-67368","marks":["code"],"text":"com.example.my-vocab.v1"},{"id":"spn-67369","text":"). The protocol does not require registration."}]},{"id":"blk-57725","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67370","text":"7. Non-goals"}]},{"id":"blk-57726","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67371","text":"Explicit, so the protocol stays small:"}]},{"id":"blk-57727","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57729","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67372","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a graph visualization protocol."},{"id":"spn-67373","text":" Force-directed layouts, dagre, hierarchies — out of scope. Runefort is grids only. If you need a graph, use a graph tool."}]}],"id":"blk-57728","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57731","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67374","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a state-management protocol."},{"id":"spn-67375","text":" How signals are computed, where they live, how they're transported — host's problem."}]}],"id":"blk-57730","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57733","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67376","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a workforce / supervision framework."},{"id":"spn-67377","text":" That's a *vocabulary* ("},{"id":"spn-67378","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-67379","text":"), built on top."}]}],"id":"blk-57732","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57735","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67380","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a presentation framework."},{"id":"spn-67381","text":" No theming spec, no animation spec. CSS is the renderer's job."}]}],"id":"blk-57734","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57737","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67382","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not coupled to [&], PULSE, or PRISM."},{"id":"spn-67383","text":" A "},{"id":"spn-67384","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-67385","text":" describing a recipe app is fully conformant."}]}],"id":"blk-57736","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57738","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67386","text":"8. Versioning"}]},{"id":"blk-57739","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67387","text":"Semver for the protocol itself. The top-level "},{"id":"spn-67388","marks":["code"],"text":"\"runefort\": \"0.1\""},{"id":"spn-67389","text":" field is the protocol version, NOT the renderer version."}]},{"id":"blk-57740","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57742","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67390","marks":["bold"],"text":"Major bump"},{"id":"spn-67391","text":" = breaking JSON shape change."}]}],"id":"blk-57741","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57744","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67392","marks":["bold"],"text":"Minor bump"},{"id":"spn-67393","text":" = additive (new optional fields, new reserved vocabularies, new state classes)."}]}],"id":"blk-57743","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57746","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67394","marks":["bold"],"text":"Patch"},{"id":"spn-67395","text":" = clarification only, no behavior change."}]}],"id":"blk-57745","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57747","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67396","text":"A renderer MUST refuse documents with a major version it does not support. A renderer SHOULD render documents with a higher minor version, ignoring fields it does not recognize."}]},{"id":"blk-57748","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67397","text":"9. Reference framework — "},{"id":"spn-67398","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"}]},{"id":"blk-57749","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67399","text":"The canonical browser-side reference implementation is "},{"id":"spn-67400","marks":["bold"],"text":"`@runefort/core`"},{"id":"spn-67401","text":": a small set of Web Components ("},{"id":"spn-67402","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-67403","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67404","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-room>"},{"id":"spn-67405","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67406","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-claim>"},{"id":"spn-67407","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67408","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-link>"},{"id":"spn-67409","text":") implementing this protocol with no framework dependency. ~5KB minified target. Specified in "},{"id":"spn-67410","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.core.md"},{"id":"spn-67411","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-57750","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67412","text":"Why a reference framework, not just a renderer:"}]},{"id":"blk-57751","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57753","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67413","marks":["bold"],"text":"Zero-build adoption."},{"id":"spn-67414","text":" Drop one "},{"id":"spn-67415","marks":["code"],"text":"<script type=\"module\">"},{"id":"spn-67416","text":" tag into any HTML page and the protocol is rendered. No bundler, no npm, no framework."}]}],"id":"blk-57752","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57755","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67417","marks":["bold"],"text":"Universal embedding."},{"id":"spn-67418","text":" Custom Elements work inside React, Vue, Svelte, Solid, Lit, Astro, Phoenix LiveView, Rails view templates, plain HTML. The framework adapters are ~1KB each, not full reimplementations."}]}],"id":"blk-57754","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57757","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67419","marks":["bold"],"text":"Single reactivity story."},{"id":"spn-67420","text":" Property setters on "},{"id":"spn-67421","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-67422","text":" push signal updates; rooms recompute their state class. No virtual DOM, no opinionated state library — composes with whatever the host app already uses."}]}],"id":"blk-57756","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57758","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67423","text":"Conformant alternatives may exist. "},{"id":"spn-67424","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-67425","text":" is the reference, not the only option. A pure-Phoenix-LiveView renderer or a server-rendered static-HTML emitter are both valid conformant implementations."}]},{"id":"blk-57759","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67426","text":"9.1 Authoring surfaces"}]},{"id":"blk-57760","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67427","text":"The same protocol is reachable through three authoring surfaces, all equivalent and all round-trippable:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-57762","spans":[{"id":"spn-67428","text":"Surface"}]},{"id":"blk-57763","spans":[{"id":"spn-67429","text":"Format"}]},{"id":"blk-57764","spans":[{"id":"spn-67430","text":"Use case"}]}],"id":"blk-57761","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-57765","spans":[{"id":"spn-67431","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"}]},{"id":"blk-57766","spans":[{"id":"spn-67432","text":"JSON"}]},{"id":"blk-57767","spans":[{"id":"spn-67433","text":"Programmatic generation, tooling integration, canonical persistence"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57768","spans":[{"id":"spn-67434","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-*>"},{"id":"spn-67435","text":" HTML"}]},{"id":"blk-57769","spans":[{"id":"spn-67436","text":"Custom Elements"}]},{"id":"blk-57770","spans":[{"id":"spn-67437","text":"Hand-written pages, embedding inside existing apps"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57771","spans":[{"id":"spn-67438","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-67439","text":" DSL"}]},{"id":"blk-57772","spans":[{"id":"spn-67440","text":"Curly-brace declarative"}]},{"id":"blk-57773","spans":[{"id":"spn-67441","text":"Hand-authored layouts, version control reviewability"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-57774","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67442","text":"The DSL is specified in "},{"id":"spn-67443","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.dsl.md"},{"id":"spn-67444","text":". The CLI converts losslessly between all three."}]},{"id":"blk-57775","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67445","text":"9.2 Planned tree"}]},{"id":"blk-57776","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"runefort/\n  spec/\n    runefort.protocol.md       ← this document\n    runefort.core.md           ← @runefort/core web component spec\n    runefort.dsl.md            ← .rune DSL spec\n    schema.json                ← JSON schema for runefort.json\n  packages/\n    core/                      ← @runefort/core (web components, target ≤5KB)\n    cli/                       ← runefort CLI (compile/fmt/to-rune)\n    react/                     ← @runefort/react adapter (~1KB)\n    vue/                       ← @runefort/vue adapter\n    svelte/                    ← @runefort/svelte adapter\n    liveview/                  ← @runefort/liveview adapter\n  examples/\n    no-framework/              ← raw HTML, proves \"runs anywhere\"\n    supervisor-floor/          ← the [&] use case, proves supervisor-floor.v1\n    codebase-atlas/            ← non-[&], proves genericity\n    dashboard-grid/            ← non-[&], proves genericity"},{"id":"blk-57777","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67446","text":"Two non-[&] examples are required before we cut v0.1 final. Otherwise we're an [&] dashboard with a spec attached."}]},{"id":"blk-57778","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67447","text":"9.3 Build order (v0.1)"}]},{"id":"blk-57779","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67448","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-67449","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-67450","text":" — the four web components + "},{"id":"spn-67451","marks":["code"],"text":"mount(json)"},{"id":"spn-67452","text":". Smallest meaningful artifact. 2. Playground at runefort.com — live "},{"id":"spn-67453","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-67454","text":" editor → rendered floor. The shareable demo. 3. CLI compile path — "},{"id":"spn-67455","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-67456","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-67457","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-67458","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-67459","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-67460","text":" → static HTML. 4. Adapters — React, then LiveView, then others as demand appears."}]},{"id":"blk-57780","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67461","text":"Adapters wait until non-zero users exist. Shipping all adapters before having users is the wrong direction of optimization."}]},{"id":"blk-57781","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67462","text":"10. Relationship to the [&] stack"}]},{"id":"blk-57782","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67463","text":"Runefort is "},{"id":"spn-67464","marks":["bold"],"text":"independent of"},{"id":"spn-67465","text":" [&]. It does not import, depend on, or require any [&] protocol. However:"}]},{"id":"blk-57783","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57785","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67466","marks":["code"],"text":"[&]"},{"id":"spn-67467","text":" capability descriptors MAY be embedded in "},{"id":"spn-67468","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-67469","text":" under "},{"id":"spn-67470","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-67471","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-57784","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57787","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67472","text":"PULSE manifest phases MAY drive room generation in tooling that bridges PULSE → Runefort."}]}],"id":"blk-57786","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57789","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67473","text":"PRISM scores MAY be a signal source for state bindings."}]}],"id":"blk-57788","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57790","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67474","text":"These are *integration patterns*, not protocol requirements. A Runefort layout that knows nothing about [&] is fully conformant."}]},{"id":"blk-57791","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67475","text":"11. Open questions for v0.2"}]},{"id":"blk-57792","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57794","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67476","marks":["bold"],"text":"Nesting."},{"id":"spn-67477","text":" A room inside a room (zoomable). Worth adding to core, or push to a vocabulary?"}]}],"id":"blk-57793","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57796","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67478","marks":["bold"],"text":"Streaming layout edits."},{"id":"spn-67479","text":" Today the JSON is whole-document. Should there be a patch format?"}]}],"id":"blk-57795","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57798","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67480","marks":["bold"],"text":"Manifest discovery."},{"id":"spn-67481","text":" Does a renderer auto-discover "},{"id":"spn-67482","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-67483","text":" in a repo, or is the path always provided?"}]}],"id":"blk-57797","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57800","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67484","marks":["bold"],"text":"Multiple anchors per room."},{"id":"spn-67485","text":" Today one anchor. Real codebases have N files per logical region."}]}],"id":"blk-57799","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57801","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67486","text":"These are explicitly deferred. v0.1 ships with the four primitives and nothing else."}]},{"id":"blk-57802","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67487","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57803","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67488","text":"*This spec is the contract. Everything in "},{"id":"spn-67489","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.com/docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-67490","text":" (the spatial-cognition / dark-factory spec) is now reframed as the "},{"id":"spn-67491","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-67492","text":" vocabulary plus the "},{"id":"spn-67493","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.dark_factory"},{"id":"spn-67494","text":" reference application — both built on top of this protocol.*"}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierahmljogwejhcuphxzdudxbqrf7s3gj4vm6aamg6kcxykz4hfpyo6a","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}